{
  "schema_version": "1.7.0",
  "id": "USN-9115-1",
  "summary": "mxml vulnerabilities",
  "details": "It was discovered that Mini-XML used unbounded recursion when deleting and\nwriting XML nodes. An attacker could possibly use these issues to cause\nMini-XML to crash, resulting in a denial of service. These issues only\naffected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS. (CVE-2016-4570, CVE-2016-4571)\n\nIt was discovered that Mini-XML incorrectly handled certain floating point\nvalues when writing XML nodes, leading to a stack-based buffer overflow. An\nattacker could possibly use this issue to cause Mini-XML to crash,\nresulting in a denial of service, or possibly execute arbitrary code.\n(CVE-2018-20004)",
